        "text": {
            "description_html": "<b>Narrow Stile Crash Bar Exit Device</b>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\nGlobal Series TH1100-ED crash bar\u001d style exit devices are suitable for narrow, medium or wide stile aluminum and hollow metal doors including narrow stile store front glass doors.\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\nThey have a contoured cross bar that will fit doors up to 42\" wide and can be field sized to accommodate narrow doors.\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n<b>\r\nFeatures and Specifications</b> for the Global TH1100-ED Narrow Stile Crash Bar Exit Device:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Material: Contoured anodized aluminum cross bar, stainless steel springs</li>\r\n<li>Latch: 1-1/4\" wide x 7-1/4\" long with 1/2\" stainless throw</li>\r\n<li>Backset: 1-5/32\" from edge of door to center line of device</li>\r\n<li>Strike: Rim mounted roller strike with shim</li>\r\n<li>Projection: 4-3/4\"</li>\r\n<li>Stile: 1-7/8\" minimum</li>\r\n<li>Handing: Handed</li>\r\n<li>Door Thickness: 1-3/4\" - 2-1/4\"</li>\r\n<li>Door Width: Up to 42\"</li>\r\n<li>Mounting Height: Recommended installation at 39-13/32\" from floor to center line of latch or strike assemblies</li>\r\n<li>Fasteners: Furnished with sheet metal, machine screws and shoulder mounting studs with set screws</li>\r\n<li>Cylinder: Optional <a href=\"/products/store-front-door-rim-cylinder-global-th1100-rcb\"><b>Rim Cylinder</b></a> or <a href=\"/products/high-security-rim-cylinder-with-horizontal-tail-piece-mul-t-lock-206sp-rim1ht-xx\"><b>Mul-T-Lock High Security Rim Cylinder</b></a></li>\r\n<li>Dogging: Inside - push up dog pin rotate with screw driver, Outside - by optional <a href=\"/products/store-front-door-rim-cylinder-global-th1100-rcb\"><b>Key Rim Cylinder</b></a></li>\r\n<li>Grade 2</li>\r\n<li><b>UL Listed for Panic Hardware</b></li></li>\r\n<li>Warranty: 10 Years</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\nThis Exit Device is available in Aluminum or Dark Bronze finish. \r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n<b>*Important</b> When selecting <b>Door Hand</b> for this exit device: \r\n<br>\r\n1. Stand on the <b>Push Side</b> of the door, facing the door. <br>\r\n2. If the \"Pivot Hinge\" is on your \"Left\", choose \"Left Hand Door\". <br>\r\n3. If the \"Pivot Hinge\" is on your \"Right\", choose \"Right Hand Door\". <br>\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0766/1489/3857/files/closer-handing.gif?v=1704354510\"  width=\"410\" height=\"195\" border=\"0\"alt=\"door handing\">\r\n</p>",
